    "reviewNotes": "Both agents failed to fulfill their assigned roles. Openspec was instructed to elaborate the empty acceptance criteria and add technical depth, but reports acceptanceChanged:false and splitCount:0 — it derived criteria in notes only without persisting them. Speckit's notes claim it 'added' edge-case criteria (casing, determinism, type, whitespace) yet also reports acceptanceChanged:false, a direct contradiction. Either the criteria were applied (acceptanceChanged should be true) or they were not (notes are misleading). The two agents' contributions overlap conceptually — both merely re-derived intent from the title without producing durable spec artifacts. Human review needed to determine whether AC elaboration was actually written somewhere outside the contribution notes, or if the pipeline silently dropped both agents' outputs.",
